          "caption": "Nevada City Firehouse No. 1 in Nevada City, California, on May 31, 2020. Completed in the spring of 1861, this firehouse was home to Nevada Hose Company No.1 from 1861 to 1938. The brick building originally had a much simpler facade of the Greek revival style, with a tall bell tower. In the early part of the twentieth century, the facade was replaced by the present Victorian gingerbread front.",
